---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="What is this site?"
  description="The Electricity Authority's market files are public, and built for market systems. This page covers how New Zealand's electricity market works, and what Gridwatch is."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>What is this site?</h1>
    <p>
      The Electricity Authority publishes the files for New Zealand's wholesale
      electricity market, and anyone can download them. They're a slog if you
      don't already work in the industry, because they were written for the
      systems that run the market.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Authority is the public body that sets the market's rules, and the
      files are on a site it calls Electricity Market Information, or EMI.
      Gridwatch reads those files and makes pages from them for anyone curious
      about how New Zealand's energy market works.
    </p>
    <h2>The bill and the wholesale market</h2>
    <p>
      Power stations don't bill households. They offer electricity in bulk into
      a wholesale market, and retailers buy it there. A retailer is the company
      named on a household bill.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wholesale prices are set in short slices of the day. A half-hour price, or
      a spot price, is the wholesale number in one of those slices, not a long
      contract, and it can move a long way from one slice to the next. A
      household bill is a retail plan, so it doesn't normally jump the same way,
      because most household plans don't pass every wholesale spike through.
    </p>
    <figure class="diagram">
      <figcaption>From power stations to a household bill</figcaption>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>
          <strong>Power stations</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wholesale market</strong>
          <span class="flow-edge">sell in bulk</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Retailer</strong>
          <span class="flow-edge">retailers buy</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Household</strong>
          <span class="flow-edge">household bill</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
    <h2>Who publishes the files, who runs the grid</h2>
    <p>
      EMI is the Authority's public record of the market. The files are
      complete, though places still show up as station codes, and each kind of
      record lives in its own file, which rarely says why a number moved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Running the high-voltage network is a different job. Transpower is the
      system operator, the organisation that keeps that network working from
      minute to minute. The Authority sets the rules and publishes EMI,
      Transpower runs the grid, and this site is separate from both. Gridwatch
      reads the EMI files after the day is over.
    </p>
    <h2>North Island and South Island</h2>
    <p>
      A cable under Cook Strait carries power between the North Island and the
      South Island. That link does not make them one market all the time. If the
      cable can't carry enough, or one island is short of power, prices on one
      side can pull away from the other.
    </p>
    <h2>Dry years and still days</h2>
    <p>
      New Zealand gets a lot of its electricity from hydro lakes and from wind.
      Lakes run low in a dry year, which means other stations have to make up
      the difference, and wholesale prices tend to rise. Wind farms produce less
      on still days, so the market has to find the electricity somewhere else.
      Those conditions show up in the files this site reads.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site looks at</h2>
    <p>
      Gridwatch looks at days that have already finished, so tomorrow's prices
      aren't in these files. For an official source file, go to
      <a href="https://www.emi.ea.govt.nz/Wholesale/Datasets">EMI</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      How the pages are built is on How we do this, and what you should and
      shouldn't use the numbers for is on Terms.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure-page);
  }

  .prose > :not(.diagram) {
    max-width: var(--measure-prose);
  }

  .flow {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .flow li {
    background: var(--color-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .flow strong {
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .flow-edge {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 36rem) {
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .flow li {
      position: relative;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 4px solid var(--color-brand);
    }

    .flow li:not(:last-child)::after {
      content: "→";
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      right: calc(var(--space-3) / -2);
      color: var(--color-ink-muted);
      font-size: var(--text-heading);
      line-height: 1;
      transform: translate(50%, -50%);
    }
  }
</style>
